/S /H2
/P 87 0 R
/T (Statistical vs practical significance. With about 4,000 wines even tiny effects give very small p-values, so p-values alone do not show strength. The effect sizes \(r = 0.46, d = 1.13\) show the alcohol difference is meaningful in practice. But alcohol explains only 21% of the variation in quality, and the tests show association, not causation.)
/E (Statistical vs practical significance. With about 4,000 wines even tiny effects give very small p-values, so p-values alone do not show strength. The effect sizes \(r = 0.46, d = 1.13\) show the alcohol difference is meaningful in practice. But alcohol explains only 21% of the variation in quality, and the tests show association, not causation.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [45]
>>
