/T (The data are imbalanced \(about 3.8 to 1\). A model that always answers 'Not Good' would be right 79.17% of the time while finding no good wines, so accuracy alone is misleading and precision, recall, F1 and ROC-AUC are used as well. The split was stratified, so both sets keep the same class proportions. The original quality column was removed from the predictors, because the label is derived from it and keeping it would cause target leakage.)
