456 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 95 0 R
/E (The project followed a complete workflow: data understanding, cleaning, exploration, hypothesis testing, OLS modelling, regression, classification, interpretation and a dashboard. Alcohol is the strongest and most consistent factor related to wine quality, followed by volatile acidity, density and chlorides. The Random Forest is the best predictive model \(regression RMSE 0.762, R2 0.291; classification F1 0.50, ROC-AUC 0.83\), but the chemical measurements explain only part of the quality score, so the models are best used as a decision-support aid and not as a replacement for expert tasting.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1 3 2]
>>
endobj
