851 0 obj
<<
/Title (Most useful variables. Alcohol is clearly the most important variable in both models \(about three times the importance of the next variable in regression\). Volatile acidity and residual sugar follow in regression; density and chlorides follow in classification. Differences among the weaker variables are small and should not be over-interpreted.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 777 0 R
/Next 899 0 R
>>
endobj
852 0 obj
<<
/Title (Recommendation: use the Random Forest for prediction in both tasks. Use the OLS model without density when the goal is to explain how each chemical property relates to quality. Predictions should be treated as a guide, not as a precise quality score.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 777 0 R
/Prev 899 0 R
>>
endobj
