/Title (Association vs predictive importance. An OLS coefficient describes the association between a variable and quality while the other variables are held constant, in the sample. Permutation importance measures how much the model's accuracy on unseen data depends on the variable. Density and residual sugar have large OLS coefficients \(-0.34 and +0.33\) with opposite signs because they are highly collinear, but they add little to prediction \(0.030 and 0.062\). Alcohol is the dependable finding: large in both views.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
